  "excluded": [
    "`Object.freeze`, `Object.assign` and `ids.forEach` are calls on builtins or an untyped receiver, not first-party functions.",
    "`module.exports = make()` calls `make` at module level, where there is no caller to hang a CALLS edge on.",
    "`mixin(exports, \u2026)` and `Reflect.defineProperty(exports, \u2026)` are top-level calls with no caller to hang a CALLS edge on; `Reflect.defineProperty` is a builtin.",
    "`renamed.js` has no refusal of its own. The wrong edge there, `client.go \u2192 ts:renamed.Handler.run`, names a node no file declares, so the existence check refuses it alone and no rule of the export map is tested by it (the fifth review's N5). `decoyed.js` is the same shape with a decoy `class Handler`, where ignoring the rename does emit an edge."
